From 9aa0aafb2d1623e2b480b35307373bc3f34ee90c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Di Yao <di.yao@vanderbilt.edu>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 09:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix: pass the model dtype to get_extended_attention_mask by
 keyword

0001 meant to hand this call the dtype of the model weights rather than the
device object, but left the value in the third positional slot, and the
signature is get_extended_attention_mask(attention_mask, input_shape, device,
dtype). The dtype lands in `device`, so every forward pass prints

  FutureWarning: The `device` argument is deprecated and will be removed in
  v5 of Transformers.

The mask came out right regardless. The text encoder has is_decoder=False, so
transformers never reads `device`, and dtype=None falls back to self.dtype,
which is already next(self.parameters()).dtype. Naming the argument costs
nothing, makes the call do what 0001 said it did, and takes it off the list of
things v5 removes.
---
 groundingdino/models/GroundingDINO/bertwarper.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/groundingdino/models/GroundingDINO/bertwarper.py b/groundingdino/models/GroundingDINO/bertwarper.py
index 045b44d..b016240 100644
--- a/groundingdino/models/GroundingDINO/bertwarper.py
+++ b/groundingdino/models/GroundingDINO/bertwarper.py
@@ -116,7 +116,7 @@ class BertModelWarper(nn.Module):
         model_dtype = next(self.parameters()).dtype
         
         extended_attention_mask: torch.Tensor = self.get_extended_attention_mask(
-            attention_mask, input_shape, model_dtype
+            attention_mask, input_shape, dtype=model_dtype
         )
 
         # If a 2D or 3D attention mask is provided for the cross-attention
